<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea to release 700 bln won through repo.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea to release 700 bln won through repo.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea said on Monday it would supply 700 billion won to the banking system through two-day repurchase agreements (repos).  </p>
<p>A central bank official said the bank had decided to increase money supply to help domestic banks meet a twice-monthly deadline for won reserve requirements due on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Bank of Korea plans tenders for the repos at 0450 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
